\fs96 \cf2 mojo doc\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa400\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Compiles docstrings from a Mojo file.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa800\partightenfactor0

\fs64 \cf2 Synopsis\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf12 \cb13 mojo doc [options] <path>\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf14 \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf15 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa800\partightenfactor0

\fs64 \cf2 Description\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 This is an early version of a documentation tool that generates an API reference from Mojo code comments. Currently, it generates a structured output of all docstrings into a JSON file, and it does not generate HTML. This output format is subject to change.\
The input may be a single file or a directory. If you specify a directory, it will generate a single JSON output with documentation for all modules found in that path, recursively.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa800\partightenfactor0

\fs64 \cf2 Options\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 Output options\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs35 \cf10 \cb16 -o <PATH>
\fs40 \cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Sets the path and filename for the JSON output. If not provided, output is written to stdout.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 Compilation options\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs35 \cf10 \cb16 -I <PATH>
\fs40 \cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Appends the given path to the list of directories that Mojo will search for any package/module dependencies. That is, if the file you pass to 
\fs28 \cf10 \cb16 mojo doc
\fs32 \cf2 \cb1  imports any packages that do not reside in the local path and are not part of the Mojo standard library, use this to specify the path where Mojo can find those packages.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 Validation options\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 The following validation options help ensure that your docstrings use valid structure and meet other style criteria. By default, warnings are emitted only if the docstrings contain errors that prevent translation to the output format. (More options coming later.)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs35 \cf10 \cb16 --diagnose-missing-doc-strings
\fs40 \cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Emits diagnostic warnings for missing or partial doc strings.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs35 \cf10 \cb16 --docs-base-path <PATH>
\fs40 \cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Sets the path prefix for generated documentation links.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 Compilation diagnostic options\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Controls how the Mojo compiler outputs diagnostics related to compiling and running Mojo source code.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs35 \cf10 \cb16 --max-notes-per-diagnostic <INTEGER>
\fs40 \cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 When the Mojo compiler emits diagnostics, it sometimes also prints notes with additional information. This option sets an upper threshold on the number of notes that can be printed with a diagnostic. If not specified, the default maximum is 10.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs35 \cf10 \cb16 --Werror
\fs40 \cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Treat warnings as errors.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs35 \cf10 \cb16 --Wno-error
\fs40 \cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Do not treat warnings as errors (overrides -Werror).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs48 \cf2 Common options\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs35 \cf10 \cb16 --diagnostic-format <FORMAT>
\fs40 \cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 The format in which diagnostics and error messages are printed. Must be one of "text" or "json" ("text" is the default).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs35 \cf10 \cb16 --help
\fs40 \cf2 \cb1 , 
\fs35 \cf10 \cb16 -h
\fs40 \cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Displays help information.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs35 \cf10 \cb16 --help-hidden
\fs40 \cf2 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 Displays help for hidden options.\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri960\partightenfactor0
